    <innerclass refid="classschur__poly__heap" prot="public">schur_poly_heap</innerclass>
    <briefdescription>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="classschur__poly__heap" kindref="compound">schur_poly_heap</ref></computeroutput> <mdash/> geometric-bucket accumulator specialised for <computeroutput><ref refid="class_schur_ring2" kindref="compound">SchurRing2</ref></computeroutput> polynomials. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Declares <computeroutput><ref refid="classschur__poly__heap" kindref="compound">schur_poly_heap</ref></computeroutput>, a <computeroutput><ref refid="style_8hpp_a7ad908ecb2518165a3f24d63b222140e_1a7ad908ecb2518165a3f24d63b222140e" kindref="member">GEOHEAP_SIZE</ref></computeroutput> (15)-level size-quadrupling heap of <computeroutput><ref refid="unionring__elem" kindref="compound">ring_elem</ref></computeroutput> slots used by <computeroutput><ref refid="class_schur_ring2" kindref="compound">SchurRing2</ref></computeroutput> multiplication to collect the many <computeroutput>c_{lambda mu}^nu s_nu</computeroutput> intermediate terms produced by Littlewood-Richardson enumeration. <computeroutput>add(p)</computeroutput> drops <computeroutput><ref refid="godbolt_test_8cpp_a533391314665d6bf1b5575e9a9cd8552_1a533391314665d6bf1b5575e9a9cd8552" kindref="member">p</ref></computeroutput> into the smallest level whose <computeroutput><ref refid="engine_8cpp_a7f0014af4839bb515bdfe826ce4a7bcb_1a7f0014af4839bb515bdfe826ce4a7bcb" kindref="member">heap_size</ref>[i]</computeroutput> threshold it fits under (the same <computeroutput>4, 16, 64, ..., 1073741824</computeroutput> table from <computeroutput><ref refid="engine_8cpp" kindref="compound">engine.cpp</ref></computeroutput>, each level four times the previous) and cascades on overflow; <computeroutput>value()</computeroutput> flattens the tower into a single canonical sum and resets the heap. Sizing the threshold to each slot&apos;s current term count amortises the LR collection away from the quadratic merge a naive term-by-term accumulator would walk.</para>
<para>The shape mirrors the engine&apos;s other geometric heaps (<computeroutput><ref refid="gbring_8hpp" kindref="compound">gbring.hpp</ref></computeroutput>&apos;s <computeroutput><ref refid="classgbvector_heap" kindref="compound">gbvectorHeap</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="geovec_8hpp" kindref="compound">geovec.hpp</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="geopoly_8hpp" kindref="compound">geopoly.hpp</ref></computeroutput>) but the slot type is the <computeroutput><ref refid="unionring__elem" kindref="compound">ring_elem</ref></computeroutput> of the owning <computeroutput><ref refid="class_schur_ring2" kindref="compound">SchurRing2</ref> *S</computeroutput> <mdash/> <computeroutput>add_to</computeroutput> calls <computeroutput>S-&gt;add(a, b)</computeroutput> and assigns <computeroutput>S-&gt;<ref refid="godbolt_test_8cpp_a627f44b64b5d8d3ae8cb6a675f164405_1a627f44b64b5d8d3ae8cb6a675f164405" kindref="member">zero()</ref></computeroutput> to the drained slot. Only <computeroutput><ref refid="schur2_8cpp" kindref="compound">schur2.cpp</ref></computeroutput> consumes this header: the LR-multiplication driver allocates an <computeroutput>SMheap</computeroutput> of this type, calls <computeroutput>add</computeroutput> for each output term, and reads <computeroutput>value()</computeroutput> once at the end.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="schur2_8hpp" kindref="compound">schur2.hpp</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="geopoly_8hpp" kindref="compound">geopoly.hpp</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="geovec_8hpp" kindref="compound">geovec.hpp</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
